From bbb682e47ff4faf61185f0475fad820a34403cc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WilbertACDX <115293547+WilbertACDX@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 02:47:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] MSVC: drop the unused <dirent.h> include

FATStorage.cpp includes it but never calls anything from it -- every
directory operation in the file goes through FatFs (f_opendir/f_readdir),
not POSIX dirent. MSVC has no <dirent.h>, and melonDS's own CMake expects
one to be findable on Windows when not building with MinGW, which is only
true if you happen to have a shim installed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/FATStorage.cpp | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/FATStorage.cpp b/src/FATStorage.cpp
index c93e90b..decff34 100644
--- a/src/FATStorage.cpp
+++ b/src/FATStorage.cpp
@@ -17,7 +17,6 @@
 */
 
 #include <string.h>
-#include <dirent.h>
 #include <inttypes.h>
 #include <vector>
 
-- 
2.44.0.windows.1

